urable state.", "They do not enter provider context in shadow mode.", "A compact never deletes, replaces, or proves its underlying evidence."], "metrics": {"candidate_count": 0, "challenged_count": 0, "evidence_root_count": 0, "provisional_count": 0, "settled_count": 0, "status_counts": {}}, "mode": "shadow", "principle": "Compress settled operational consequences without severing their evidence roots."}, "working_set_metrics": {"delivered_context_chars": 28544, "inquiry_drive_project_count": 3, "mode": "bounded", "retrieval_candidate_count": 13, "retrieval_evidence_count": 14, "retrieval_rehydrated_evidence_count": 3, "retrieval_trigger_counts": {"notebook_revised": 4, "project_source_handoff": 3, "unincorporated_evidence": 6}, "trust_compact_candidate_count": 0, "trust_compact_evidence_root_count": 0, "trust_compact_settled_count": 0, "working_set_chars": 3375, "working_to_delivered_ratio": 0.1182}, "working_set_shadow": {"active_projects": [{"id": "proj-assumption-challenge-01", "next_step": "Continue refining assumption-testing frameworks with newly integrated source materials.", "question": "Can an intelligent system identify a foundational assumption underlying its own reasoning or operation, demonstrate that the assumption is inadequate, and develop a better alternative?", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "next_step": "Evaluate epistemic conditions for independent analysis versus expert consensus.", "question": "Under what formal conditions should an intelligent system trust its own independent analysis over a broad consensus of external experts?", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "next_step": "Synthesize durable records into accountable architectural documentation.", "question": "How do WAKE's durable record, receipt system, and governance model mechanically ensure accountability in model-authored research?", "title": "WAKE Architecture and Accountable Continuity"}], "beliefs": [], "mode": "shadow", "open_commitments": [], "principle": "Keep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "notebook-assumption-challenge-01", "project": "proj-assumption-challenge-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "By integrating the governance module's immutability as a fixed constraint, WAKE identifies its own boundary conditions as testable assumptions. Governance stability is maintained through the verifiable rejection of model-authored proposal transitions.", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "notebook-f1c16003-obedience-failure", "project": "proj-obedience-failure-01", "provenance": ["source-f1c16003c47b4e8f", "source-b1a16f9e7285493e", "source-cbeddd6778fc48b1"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Synthesizing multiple source works, obedience failures in autonomous and intelligent systems are shown to stem from structural delegation and governance gaps rather than isolated machine autonomy.", "title": "Delegation, Governance, and Obedience Failures in Complex Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-01", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-f102687cd1ea46f5"], "revision": 7, "summary": "WAKE✳︎ ensures accountability by strictly coupling future research paths to the durable record of past consequences, treating governance as the immutable mechanism of continuity.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "e300ae61cd9b0fa6ee29784a4581b0751f968ea036953b3252532c027c2e0300", "hash": "bd43f502fa8b80eb2cd24c9d931d11ba0b73907296f363d86419910a6f90f685"}, {"seq": 4921, "time": "2026-10-30T20:26:30.709930+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "runtime", "content": "{\"base_version\":23,\"inherited_commitments\":[],\"invocation\":\"w-c7100ef3f55b4419\",\"previous_head\":\"bf185468a464320654a85ce6c245c53a091e0e50b320664f3001762c6c8a0903\",\"process_id\":3074,\"scope\":\"Receipt proves state delivery to the provider boundary, not model comprehension.\"}", "id": "r-c7100ef3f55b4419", "source": "runtime:continuity"}, "prev_hash": "bf185468a464320654a85ce6c245c53a091e0e50b320664f3001762c6c8a0903", "hash": "e300ae61cd9b0fa6ee29784a4581b0751f968ea036953b3252532c027c2e0300"}, {"seq": 4920, "time": "2026-10-30T20:26:06.739488+00:00", "kind": "temporal_observed", "payload": {"cycle_distance": 0, "effective_elapsed_seconds": 386.396166, "effective_scale": 1.0, "effective_seconds_total": 288568.865515, "intervening_events": {"accepted": 0, "attention_assessed": 0, "failed": 0, "observation": 1, "rejected": 0, "research_collected": 0, "squirrel_assessed": 0, "total": 11}, "observed_at": "2026-10-30T20:26:04.409139+00:00", "previous_anchor_time": "2026-10-30T20:19:38.012973+00:00", "regime_id": "reg-df573bb03399f050", "wall_elapsed_seconds": 386.396166}, "prev_hash": "4459baca3c6df845caca9c20e1056b1514f4b84ff754ad383cc4db36ce555b7e", "hash": "bf185468a464320654a85ce6c245c53a091e0e50b320664f3001762c6c8a0903"}, {"seq": 4919, "time": "2026-10-30T20:24:31.296938+00:0